+# Symtropy Documentation Changelog — v2.9
+
+Date: 2026-07-21
+
+## Added
+
+- large-carrier multirole and non-specialization contract;
+- common civic core, open interfaces and mission-role envelope;
+- carrier profile schema;
+- eight hull-lineage grammars and internal city atlas;
+- nested carriers, base-carriers, mobile homes and field vehicles;
+- access, qualification, ownership, charter and command progression;
+- industrial construction, yards, suppliers, certification and commissioning;
+- crew stations, NPC delegation, automation and graceful degradation;
+- ten multirole carrier family profiles, including ocean and hostile-world carriers;
+- benchmark schema, fixture and one-hundred-ticket backlog;
+- v2.9 registry, dependency map, roadmap and readiness matrix.
+
+## Corrected Direction
+
+Earlier carrier concepts could be read as single-purpose classes. v2.9 makes each large carrier a broad civilization with a common baseline and configurable emphasis. Family names now identify lineages and customary profiles rather than exclusive capabilities.
+
+## Evidence
+
+All new capabilities remain D3 / I0 until representative implementation and benchmark evidence exist.
