+# Canon Registry and Document Governance
+
+## Purpose
+
+Integrate v2.9 large-carrier decisions without replacing the Firstlight and Continuance production spine or converting spacecraft into single-role classes, personal loot or scenery inhabited by people without agency.
+
+# v2.9 Ownership
+
+[Large Carrier Multirole Civilization and Non-Specialization Contract](./LARGE_CARRIER_MULTIROLE_CIVILIZATION_AND_NON_SPECIALIZATION_CONTRACT_V0_1.md) owns the common civic baseline, mission-emphasis model and variety boundaries.
+
+[Carrier Access, Ownership, Charter, Command, and Crew Sovereignty Contract](./CARRIER_ACCESS_OWNERSHIP_CHARTER_COMMAND_AND_CREW_SOVEREIGNTY_CONTRACT_V0_1.md) owns progression, property, authority, command legitimacy and resident rights.
+
+[Large Carrier Common Core, Open Interfaces, and Role Envelope Runtime](../tech/LARGE_CARRIER_COMMON_CORE_OPEN_INTERFACES_AND_ROLE_ENVELOPE_RUNTIME_V0_1.md) owns component graphs, capacity domains, standard interfaces, profile allocation and configuration.
+
+[Nested Vehicle Ecology, Docking, Deployment, and Base-Carrier Runtime](../tech/NESTED_VEHICLE_ECOLOGY_DOCKING_DEPLOYMENT_AND_BASE_CARRIER_RUNTIME_V0_1.md) owns carriers of carriers, persistent mobile-home identity and deployment.
+
+[Carrier Construction Yards, Supply Chains, Certification, and Commissioning Runtime](../tech/CARRIER_CONSTRUCTION_YARDS_SUPPLY_CHAINS_CERTIFICATION_AND_COMMISSIONING_RUNTIME_V0_1.md) owns player-buildability at industrial scale.
+
+[Carrier Crew, Automation, Stations, Damage, and Graceful Degradation Runtime](../tech/CARRIER_CREW_AUTOMATION_STATIONS_DAMAGE_AND_GRACEFUL_DEGRADATION_RUNTIME_V0_1.md) owns operations, delegation, station play and survivable failure.
+
+[Large Carrier Hull Lineages, Cultural Variety, and Internal City Atlas](../lore/LARGE_CARRIER_HULL_LINEAGES_CULTURAL_VARIETY_AND_INTERNAL_CITY_ATLAS_V0_1.md) owns structural and cultural variation.
+
+[Multirole Carrier Families, Mission Profiles, and World Adaptation Atlas](../lore/MULTIROLE_CARRIER_FAMILIES_MISSION_PROFILES_AND_WORLD_ADAPTATION_ATLAS_V0_1.md) owns the ten reference families as emphases rather than classes.
+
+[Large Carrier Ownership, Build, Multirole, and Command Benchmark](../ops/LARGE_CARRIER_OWNERSHIP_BUILD_AND_COMMAND_BENCHMARK_V0_1.md) owns promotion evidence.
+
+# v2.9 Canonical Decisions
+
+- Large carriers are broad civilizations with mission emphases.
+- All inhabited large carriers retain a common civic and operational baseline.
+- Shared interfaces do not require shared silhouettes or cultures.
+- Carrier families are lineages and customary profiles, not exclusive classes.
+- Mobile homes remain persistent identities while nested inside larger craft.
+- Access, qualification, authority, ownership and command are separate progressions.
+- Meaningful carrier participation begins long before ownership.
+- Civilization carriers are normally built through institutions, yards and multi-year campaigns.
+- Command coordinates autonomous people and departments; it does not own them.
+- Automation compresses routine but cannot erase political and ethical decisions.
+- Damage produces graceful degradation, changed mission and history.
+- The first proof remains bounded and may not displace Firstlight or Continuance implementation.
+
+# Canonical Decision Spine
+
+1. [Symtropy Game Constitution v0.6](./SYMTROPY_GAME_CONSTITUTION_V0_6.md)
+2. [Breaking of Firstlight Contract](./BREAKING_OF_FIRSTLIGHT_LOSS_CONTINUITY_AND_PLAYER_AGENCY_CONTRACT_V0_1.md)
+3. [Mobile Continuance Base Contract](./MOBILE_CONTINUANCE_BASE_HOME_VEHICLE_AND_CREW_SOVEREIGNTY_CONTRACT_V0_1.md)
+4. [Large Carrier Multirole Contract](./LARGE_CARRIER_MULTIROLE_CIVILIZATION_AND_NON_SPECIALIZATION_CONTRACT_V0_1.md)
+5. [Carrier Ownership and Command Contract](./CARRIER_ACCESS_OWNERSHIP_CHARTER_COMMAND_AND_CREW_SOVEREIGNTY_CONTRACT_V0_1.md)
+6. [System Interaction and Dependency Map v2.2](./SYSTEM_INTERACTION_AND_DEPENDENCY_MAP_V2_2.md)
+7. [Game Implementation Roadmap v2.2](../ops/GAME_IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP_V2_2.md)
+8. [Implementation Readiness Matrix v2.2](../ops/SYMTROPY_IMPLEMENTATION_READINESS_MATRIX_V2_2.md)
+9. [Large Carrier Benchmark](../ops/LARGE_CARRIER_OWNERSHIP_BUILD_AND_COMMAND_BENCHMARK_V0_1.md)
+
+# Evidence Boundary
+
+All v2.9 systems remain D3 / I0. The documents define intended behavior but do not prove simulation, performance, UI, networking, variety, player comprehension or fun.
+
+## Registry Maxim
+
+> **A carrier enters canon as a civilization only when the documentation remembers both what the hull can do and who has the right to decide what it should do.**
