+# System Interaction and Dependency Map
+
+## Core Spine
+
+```text
+world and mission need
+→ charter, ownership and requirements
+→ hull lineage and common-core capacity
+→ yard, supply chains and construction
+→ districts, residents and institutions
+→ carried mobile-base ecology
+→ qualification, automation and command
+→ deployment, travel, work and emergency
+→ damage, refit and historical transformation
+→ successor mission and carrier identity
+```
+
+# Required Dependencies
+
+## Spacecraft physics
+
+Mass, inertia, propulsion, power, thermal rejection, pressure, radiation and trajectory remain authoritative.
+
+## Closed-loop habitat
+
+Population, atmosphere, water, food, waste, disease and ecology determine true endurance.
+
+## Mobile-home lineage
+
+Crawlers, submarines, flotillas and other homes retain identity while embarked.
+
+## Construction and economy
+
+Yards, materials, labor, finance, certification and maintenance make buildability real.
+
+## NPC work and institutions
+
+Departments require people, qualifications, schedules, authority and professional ethics.
+
+## Governance and justice
+
+Title, command, resident rights, emergency authority, refusal and succession remain separate.
+
+## Networking and worldline truth
+
+Docking, ownership, damage and configuration are authoritative and cannot duplicate during locality transfer.
+
+## Symthaea direction
+
+Symthaea may surface meaningful operations and emergencies from true state. It may not invent failures, crew disobedience or vulnerabilities for drama.
+
+# Scale Transitions
+
+```text
+field vehicle
+↕ mobile home
+↕ base-carrier
+↕ civilization carrier
+↕ station, route or seed convoy
+```
+
+Each transition preserves people, cargo, damage, authority and history.
+
+# Carrier Profile Flow
+
+```text
+common civic core
++ hull lineage
++ mission emphasis vector
++ installed modules
++ carried-base mix
++ residents and charter
++ damage and repair ancestry
+= current carrier configuration
+```
+
+No label alone grants capability.
+
+# First Implementation Dependency Order
+
+1. authoritative carrier identity;
+2. twelve common-core domains;
+3. one hull and three mission profiles;
+4. one dock and one mobile-home identity;
+5. bounded station operation and NPC delegation;
+6. ownership and authority ledger;
+7. one construction proof;
+8. one graceful-degradation emergency;
+9. second hull lineage and blind variety study;
+10. wider carrier family content.
+
+# Production Boundary
+
+The carrier stack depends on a playable Continuance Crawler, persistent residents and basic spacecraft locality. Carrier work may develop schemas and isolated prototypes earlier, but should not become the critical path for the first playable release.
+
+## Map Maxim
+
+> **The large ship is where vehicle physics, household life, industrial production and political legitimacy become one system. None may be replaced by the others.**
